abstract: >-
  The Federated Analytics Ontology is a collaborative effort to
  develop shared language for federated analytics in UK health
  data research. It defines concepts for a range of audiences —
  including public, technical, researcher and governance — and
  maps each against the Five Safes, FAIR, PEDRI and SATRE
  frameworks. This work has been shaped by extensive public
  engagement and contributions from advisory groups committed to
  ethical, transparent, and accountable health data research.
